# bsim4va tests

We use the same test cases as for the Berkeley BSIM model (see gnucap-models/bsim/tests/b4_*.gc).

If test results with the Berkeley model (C source) and Cogenda model
(Verilog-AMS source) match within numerical tolerance, this provides a strong
sanity check for both the Gnucap model generator and the simulator.

## Test variations

$ make check TEST_PARAMSET_SELECT=compiled # default
tests compiled paramsets, bsim4_{n,p}mos.so

$ make check TEST_PARAMSET_SELECT=interpreted
tests interpreted paramset based on generic model

## Ratings

Each test result is rated according to is level of agreement with the official benchmark output files `bsim/BSIM481/benchmark_test/*.out`.

+ Basic sanity check passed - result appears physically reasonable
++ Good qualitative match with benchmark
+++ Quantative match up to numerical tolerance

### DC sweeps
```
b4_test1.gc  +++
b4_test2.gc  +++
b4_test3.gc  +++
b4_test4.gc  +++
b4_test5.gc  +++
b4_test6.gc  +++
b4_test7.gc  +++
b4_test8.gc  +++
b4_test9.gc  +++
b4_test10.gc +++
b4_test11.gc +++
b4_test12.gc +++
b4_test13.gc +++
b4_test14.gc +++
```
### AC tests
```
b4_gstage.gc +++
b4_opamp.gc ++
```
### Trans tests
```
b4_oneshot.gc +
b4_comprt.gc +
b4_comprt_tr1.gc ++
b4_oneshot_tr1.gc +
b4_oneshot_tr01.gc ++
b4_oneshot_tr001.gc ++
b4_comprt_tr1.gc ++
b4_ro_17.gc +
b4_ro_17_tr1.gc +
b4_ro_17_tr01.gc ++
b4_ro_17_tr001.gc ++
```
### Notes

- For transient test cases `b4_comprt.gc`, `b4_oneshot.gc` and `b4_ro_17.gc` a small truncation error (trtol <= 1) is required for the simulation results of the Cogenda model to converge to Berkeley model. 
